### Phase 4 — Light Mode Text Readability Across All Components

Ensure **all text is dark, bold, and perfectly readable** on the cream `#f7f5f0` background.

---

#### 4.1 Strengthen Text Across All Sections

Every component currently uses `text-muted2` (now `#1e1a12`) for body text, which is strong. However, several components use `font-light` weight which weakens readability. Changes:

| Component | Issue | Fix |
|-----------|-------|-----|
| About | Body text `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` or `font-medium` |
| Services | Card descriptions `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| Expertise | Descriptions `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| Career | Description/org `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| Philosophy | Principle text `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| ThoughtLeadership | Body `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| Contact | Description `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |
| IAMOnboarding | Description `font-light` | Change to `font-normal` |

#### 4.2 Fix Responsive `text-sm md:text-[Xpx]` Pattern

Multiple components use `text-sm md:text-[10px]` which is **backwards** — `text-sm` (14px) is larger than `text-[10px]`. On mobile, text appears at 14px, then shrinks to 10px on desktop. This should be:
- Labels: `text-[10px] md:text-xs` (small → slightly larger)
- Body: `text-sm md:text-[15px]` (keep current if intentional)

**Components affected:** About, Services, Expertise, Career, Certifications, Philosophy, ThoughtLeadership, Contact, Ecosystem

